{"content":[{"c":["HARIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Priest whom King David appointed to official duties in the temple (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.8","r":"1Chr.24.8","rawR":"1Chr.24.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.8","value":"1Chr.24.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Ancestor of a Jewish family who returned from the Babylonian exile with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.32","r":"Ezra.2.32","rawR":"Ezra.2.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.32","value":"Ezra.2.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:32"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.5","r":"Neh.10.5","rawR":"Neh.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.5","value":"Neh.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:5"},"). Members of this family were guilty of marrying foreign women (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.31","r":"Ezra.10.31","rawR":"Ezra.10.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.31","value":"Ezra.10.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:31"},"), but they divorced their wives and a representative of the clan signed Ezra’s covenant (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.27","r":"Neh.10.27","rawR":"Neh.10.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.27","value":"Neh.10.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 10:27"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Ancestor of a family of priests who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.39","r":"Ezra.2.39","rawR":"Ezra.2.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.39","value":"Ezra.2.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:39"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.42","r":"Neh.7.42","rawR":"Neh.7.42","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.42","value":"Neh.7.42"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:42"},"). Some identify him with #1 above. Members of this family were guilty of marrying foreign women."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Ancestor of Malkijah. Malkijah repaired a section of the Jerusalem wall during Nehemiah’s time (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.11","r":"Neh.3.11","rawR":"Neh.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.11","value":"Neh.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:11"},"). This Harim could be the same as #2 above."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Priest who returned from the exile with Zerubbabel (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.3","r":"Neh.12.3","rawR":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.3","value":"Neh.12.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 12:3"},"; Hebrew “Rehum,” see ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). His son (or grandson) Adna is listed as a leading priest during the high priesthood of Joiakim (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.15","r":"Neh.12.15","rawR":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.15","value":"Neh.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:15"},"). Later, under Ezra, a representative of the family (probably related to #3 above) signed the covenant of faithfulness to God (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.10.5","r":"Neh.10.5","rawR":"Neh.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.10.5","value":"Neh.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Harim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 24:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.24.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.24.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.24.8"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:32","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.32","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.32","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.32"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.5","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.5","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.5"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.31","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.31","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.31"},{"anchorText":"Neh 10:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.27","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.27","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.27"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.39","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.39","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.39"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:42","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.42","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.42","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.42"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.11","rawQueryValue":"Neh.3.11","sourceRefExact":"Neh.3.11"},{"anchorText":"Neh 12:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.3","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.3","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.3"},{"anchorText":"12:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.15","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.15","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.15"},{"anchorText":"10:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.10.5","rawQueryValue":"Neh.10.5","sourceRefExact":"Neh.10.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"394282a4080defda485f0c62ccd8c47c4aa1264d00871e96a87ec76d71c6c7b7","sourceItemName":"Harim","sourceItemOrder":117,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Harim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Harim","title":"Harim","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}